  bigIdea:
    'In 1971 Diop asked UNESCO for an international meeting in Egypt where Egyptologists and Africanists would compare their evidence on who the ancient Egyptians were, and UNESCO agreed. It met in Cairo from 28 January to 3 February 1974. The official report, printed in UNESCO’s own history, records real disagreement (most experts did not accept his claim of a homogeneous population, and on the colors in Egyptian art nothing was conceded), a large measure of agreement on his and Obenga’s linguistic method, and a conclusion in the rapporteur’s own words: not all participants had prepared work comparable with the painstakingly researched contributions of Diop and Obenga, so there was a real lack of balance in the discussions.',
